    {
      "entryId": "1co-6-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "What? know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost which is in you, which ye have of God, and ye are not your own? For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's. Christian lifestyle involves holistic sanctification: physical health, temperance, modesty, and abstaining from unclean meats (Lev 11) and harmful stimulants.",
      "density": 3.3,
      "words": 68,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-12-28",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "And God hath set some in the church, first apostles, secondarily prophets, thirdly teachers, after that miracles, then gifts of healings, helps, governments, diversities of tongues. The Holy Spirit sovereignly endows believers with spiritual abilities to equip the saints and edify the body of Christ until unity in the faith and character perfection are achieved.",
      "density": 3.0321,
      "words": 55,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 29,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 8 quoted with one exception noted — the Father who subjects all. First principle: the psalm's universal subjection has a grammatical exception that guards the Trinity — all under the Son, the Son under none but the Father.",
      "density": 2.4607,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 26,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-6-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Union with a harlot makes one body — Genesis 2 governs the body's theology. First principle: the one-flesh bond is so real that its misuse is desecration; the member of Christ cannot be joined to a harlot.",
      "density": 2.3893,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Buried, risen on the third day — according to the Scriptures. First principle: the resurrection is not an appendix to the gospel but a fulfilled prediction — Jonah, Psalm 16, and Hosea 6 all said so.",
      "density": 2.3286,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-2-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The princes of this world missed who He was. First principle: the ignorance of the crucifiers was real — and their unwitting act fulfilled the hidden counsel of God against the Lord of glory.",
      "density": 2.2786,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Two unions, two destinies. First principle: the all in Christ is as definite as the all in Adam — location, not lineage, decides life; in Him is the resurrection.",
      "density": 2.1536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-55",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Hosea's taunt becomes the resurrection's victory cry. First principle: the sting was sin and the law gave it power — the cross removes the venom, and the grave loses its victory.",
      "density": 2.1464,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-51",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The mystery revealed: living saints changed with the sleeping raised. First principle: the last generation has an exemption — not sleep but change, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trump.",
      "density": 2.1393,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The wilderness generation passed through the sea under the cloud. First principle: the exodus is the church's family album — Paul reads Israel's history as the Gentile church's own lineage of warning.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The enthroned Son reigns until the last enemy is footstooled. First principle: the kingdom is present in reign and future in completion — Psalm 110 describes the process, not just the seat.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-1-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Isaiah's marvellous work levels intellectual pride. First principle: the cross is God's answer to wisdom-worship — understanding of the prudent is brought to nothing where a crucified Messiah saves.",
      "density": 2.0393,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-1-30",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Of God, in Christ Jesus — four gifts in one Person. First principle: THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS of Jeremiah is personalized: Christ Himself is each covenant gift, not merely its delivery system.",
      "density": 2,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "If Christ is not raised, the apostolic testimony collapses into perjury. First principle: the resurrection is the fact on which every apostolic witness stands or falls — a truth-claim, not a metaphor.",
      "density": 2,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 24 settles the marketplace question. First principle: the whole earth belongs to the Lord — meat bought in the shambles carries no intrinsic idolatry; ownership sanctifies inquiry.",
      "density": 1.9571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-12-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Many members, one body — each with an office. First principle: the church is not like a body but is one; particularity of members is the design of the Head.",
      "density": 1.95,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The wilderness grumblers tempted — and Paul names the tempted one Christ. First principle: the Rock followed them, and that Rock was Christ; testing God's patience with serpents has an eternal Addressee.",
      "density": 1.9429,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-9-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The treading ox lives from its labor — and the law was written for us. First principle: God's care for animals carries a human ethic; those who sow spiritual things may reap material support.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-3-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He taketh the wise in their own craftiness. First principle: the snare of cleverness is itself — Job's friend knew the proverb before Paul weaponized it against Corinthian factions.",
      "density": 1.925,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Fornication at Peor brought sudden plague. First principle: sin's judgment can be immediate and numerical — the register of Numbers 25 stands as a memorial of consequence.",
      "density": 1.875,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-32",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Paul fights beasts at Ephesus — pointless if there is no resurrection. First principle: Isaiah 22's fatalistic feast is the logical life of unbelief; resurrection hope is what makes endurance rational.",
      "density": 1.8607,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A baptism without water — cloud above, walls on either side. First principle: the crossing was an initiation into a deliverer; Christian baptism into Christ follows the same identification pattern.",
      "density": 1.8357,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Christ is risen from the dead and become the firstfruits of those who slept. First principle: resurrection is not unique to Jesus in kind — it is the first harvest of many.",
      "density": 1.8286,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Death entered by a man; resurrection enters by a Man. First principle: the parallelism is incarnational — the problem needed a human solution, and the second Adam is it.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The golden-calf orgy is quoted as idolatry's liturgy. First principle: idolatry is feasting before a substitute god — Paul applies the Exodus scene to the Lord's-table context.",
      "density": 1.7607,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Death is the final casualty of Christ's reign. First principle: Isaiah's swallowed-up death and Revelation's lake of fire bracket the campaign — the ending is already written.",
      "density": 1.7607,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-2-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The prepared things for those who love God outrun every sense. First principle: Isaiah 64's unperceived wonders are revealed by the Spirit — not to spectators, but to lovers.",
      "density": 1.7536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-10-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "They drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them, and that Rock was Christ. First principle: the wilderness provision is typologically Christological.",
      "density": 1.65,
      "words": 22,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-3-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The thoughts of the wise are vain before Him who searches. First principle: knowing thoughts is God's prerogative — the psalm of judgment levels every boastful system.",
      "density": 1.5893,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-45",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The first man Adam became a living soul; the last Adam a life-giving spirit. First principle: resurrection life is greater than creation life — and it is in Christ.",
      "density": 1.5821,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-11-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The supper cup quotes Jeremiah 31 in blood. First principle: every Communion re-proclaims the new covenant's terms — remission by blood, remembrance by command.",
      "density": 1.5143,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-5-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Christ our Passover is sacrificed for us; therefore keep the feast. First principle: the Passover lamb's death is fulfilled in Christ, reshaping Christian worship and ethics.",
      "density": 1.5071,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-54",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Death is swallowed up in victory. First principle: Isaiah 25 and Hosea 13 are fulfilled in the bodily resurrection of believers.",
      "density": 1.3821,
      "words": 21,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1co-15-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "I delivered: Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures. First principle: atonement is substitutionary and scriptural — not a bare example.",
      "density": 1.2607,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 12,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
